<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The Company operates only in one segment, namely Aluminium Castings.   2. This statement has been prepared in accordance with Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Rules, 2015 (IND AS) prescribed under Section 133 of hte Companies Act, 2013 and other recognised accounting practices and policies to the extent possible.   3. The above results have been reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at their respective meetings held on 24th and 25th July 2023.   4. The Central Government has published the Code on Social Security, 2020 and Industrial Relations Code 2023 ( the Codes ) in the Gazetter of India, interalia subsuming various existing labour and industrial laws which deals with employees including post-employment period. The effective date of the code and rule are yet to be notified. The impact of legislative changes if any will be assessed and recognised post notification of relevant position.   5. The Board of Directors have recommended final dividend of Rs. 3.75/- per equtiy share of Rs. 5/- (75%) for the financial year 2022-23 for declaration by shareholders in the ensuing Annual General Meeting . Total dividend for the financial years 2022-23 will be Rs. 6.25 per share (125%)   6. The results for the quarter ended March 31 2023 are the balancing figures between the audited figures in respect of full financial year ended March 31, 2023 and the published year- to- date figures upto the end of the quarter of the previous financial year , which was subjected to limited review, as required under the regulations.   7. Figures have been regrouped wherever necessary to make them comparable</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
